{
  "$comment": [
    "Facts taken from Google's per-method REST references, which docs/architecture.md ranks above",
    "the Discovery document. Discovery is machine-readable and is diffed weekly by spec-check;",
    "these pages are prose and were not watched at all, which is how two scope defects survived:",
    "exportExerciseTcx needing two scopes together, and six read operations accepting scopes",
    "Discovery does not list for them. Both are stated on the pages and invisible from Discovery.",
    "",
    "The scheduled check re-reads each page and compares the scope URLs it contains with the set",
    "recorded here. It reports; it never edits. A difference is a question for a human, because",
    "the answer may be to change the SDK, to change this file, or to record a new conflict.",
    "",
    "Matching is on the scope URLs the page contains, not on its markup, so a redesign of",
    "developers.google.com does not produce a false alarm. A page that stops listing any scope at",
    "all is reported as unreadable rather than as a change, since 'no scopes found' is much more",
    "likely to mean the check broke than that Google removed authorization."
  ],
  "verifiedOn": "2026-08-31",
  "methods": [
    {
      "operation": "health.users.dataTypes.dataPoints.exportExerciseTcx",
      "url": "https://developers.google.com/health/reference/rest/v4/users.dataTypes.dataPoints/exportExerciseTcx",
      "scopes": [
        "https://www.googleapis.com/auth/googlehealth.activity_and_fitness.readonly",
        "https://www.googleapis.com/auth/googlehealth.location.readonly"
      ],
      "mustContain": [
        "this specific method requires the user to provide both one of the activity_and_fitness scopes"
      ],
      "note": "The mustContain phrase is the only place the AND requirement is stated. If it disappears, the allOf in semantics.json has lost its evidence and must be re-argued, not silently kept."
    },
    {
      "operation": "health.users.dataTypes.dataPoints.list",
      "url": "https://developers.google.com/health/reference/rest/v4/users.dataTypes.dataPoints/list",
      "scopes": [
